{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Speak to Aaron.</b> For he is obligated in the commandment of kindling the lamp." "<b>Toward the face of the menorah.</b> That is, \"and it shall give light toward its face [front].\" Now the word האיר is transitive [in this form] like תאיר נרי, unlike יאירו והארץ, which is construct-linked [i.e., in construct state with what follows]. This passage is juxtaposed to teach that the divine speech occurs also at night, for there the lamp is kindled and is not extinguished."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra parses יאירו והארץ (Isaiah 60:2) differently from the phrase under discussion; I read ונסמכה as referring to the construct (סמיכות) relationship in that verse, contrasted with the free transitive use here. The phrase האיר אל is the lemma prefix to his own citation of והאיר."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:49.302696194Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}